      "analysis_policy": "Use observed presence/absence (a count>0 is presence) over the full supplied species order. All unordered plot pairs are candidates. For a pair let a be shared species, b species present only in the first and c only in the second. The specified pairwise Baselga partition is beta_sor=(b+c)/(2*a+b+c), beta_sim=min(b,c)/(a+min(b,c)), beta_sne=beta_sor-beta_sim. Rank by beta_sne/beta_sor, not by total dissimilarity, observed richness difference alone, or abundance-weighted Bray-Curtis. If a denominator is0 the relevant component/fraction is undefined; exclude undefined fractions, and return null/empty selection if all are undefined. Keep all maximum ties within1e-10. Pair IDs join the two supplied plot IDs in source index order with '|'. Components are dimensionless.",
      "scientific_scope": "Historical1982 one-hectare BCI counts of tree stems DBH>=10cm, first8 original plots and every original species column retained. This is a descriptive incidence-index decomposition, not an inferred ecological mechanism, immigration/extinction rate, unseen-species correction or current conservation recommendation. Nestedness-resultant dissimilarity is the declared index component, not a proof of a unique generative process.",
